menu "Board Common"

    config BOARD_LANDSCAPE
        bool "Landscape orientation"
        default n
        help
            Rotate the display 90 degrees for landscape orientation.

            When enabled, LVGL sees swapped dimensions (V_RES x H_RES)
            and the board init code applies the appropriate flush callback
            rotation and touch coordinate transforms.

            The convenience macros BOARD_DISP_H_RES / BOARD_DISP_V_RES
            reflect the logical (post-rotation) dimensions.

    config BOARD_CSI_AE_TARGET
        int "CSI camera fixed exposure override (0 = sensor/ISP default)"
        default 0
        range 0 1200
        help
            Fixed exposure applied once at camera start via V4L2_CID_EXPOSURE
            (csi_set_ae_target in board_pipeline_camera_csi.c). Despite the name,
            it is written STRAIGHT to the sensor's exposure register — it is not a
            normalized AE setpoint, and there is no closed AE loop unless an ISP
            IPA config is wired. So the useful range and "neutral" value are
            sensor-specific:
              - OV5647 (Waveshare P4 boards): has on-sensor AGC/AEC, so leave at 0
                and let the sensor self-adapt.
              - OV02C10 (Guition): no on-sensor AE, but the board ships an ISP IPA
                tuning file (BOARD_CAMERA_IPA_CONFIG_NAME), so a closed exposure
                loop owns this control. Leave at 0 — a fixed value here is
                overwritten within a few frames, and the driver warns if one is
                set. Tune exposure in the tuning file instead.
            Only a sensor with neither on-sensor AE nor an IPA tuning file needs a
            value here. 0 leaves the sensor/ISP default untouched; higher = brighter.

endmenu
